Privacy Policy — Uriyadi
Last updated: July 2026

This privacy policy applies to the Uriyadi mobile game ("the App"), developed and published by Selva Gurunathan ("we", "us").

Data collection
Uriyadi does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personal data.

The App does not require you to create an account or sign in.
The App does not connect to the internet to send or receive any data.
The App does not use analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs of any kind.
The App does not access your contacts, location, camera, microphone, photos, or any other personal information on your device.
The App does not share any data with third parties, because it does not collect any in the first place.
Data stored on your device
The App saves your high scores, unlocked levels, achievement progress, and settings (such as volume and language) locally on your own device, in a private file the App creates for itself. This data never leaves your device, is never transmitted anywhere, and is deleted automatically if you uninstall the App.

Permissions
The App requests the following Android permission:

Vibrate — used to provide haptic feedback during gameplay (helping you feel your way toward the hidden pot). Not used for anything else.
Children's privacy
The App does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children, because it does not collect information from anyone at all.

Changes to this policy
If this policy ever changes (for example, if a future update adds optional online features), we will update this page and the "Last updated" date above before the change takes effect in the App.

Contact
Questions about this policy can be sent to: rselvaguru@gmail.com

